# Git LFS — the site's photography and proceedings PDFs.
#
# my-app/public holds ~360 MB of images; as ordinary git blobs that dominates
# .git, makes clones slow, and will eventually hit GitHub's repository limits.
# Tracking them as LFS keeps pointer files in history and the payloads in LFS
# storage. The 5 SVGs are the small create-next-app defaults, so they stay in
# normal git.
public/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
public/**/*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
public/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
public/**/*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
public/**/*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Same extensions, in case assets are added outside public/ later.
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text